y Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="410127" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/27/410127/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I59f65b7ad6299461a38d856977d9319cf06bf2a3" commit="13a7b535513a27911021f55fd69d0c4a43c45248" commit_message="chipset-skl: extending intel_idle.max_cstate=7 for all skl systems.  PC-States higher than 7 allow assertaion of SLP_S0$ signal which in turn affects PMIC entering certain low-power modes which may be a source of platform instability. Disabling for now.  Previously we were only disabling pc[8|9|10] on SKL-Y platforms, moving to chipset-skl to disable across all SKL platforms. There is no direct control of the pc state through the driver, we indirectly limit it using the cpu c-state.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57920 TEST=manual, cat /proc/cmdline &lt;contains intel_idle.max_cstate=7&gt;  Turn off display via turning blacklight to zero. Examine SLP_S0# signal no longer asserts  Change-Id: I59f65b7ad6299461a38d856977d9319cf06bf2a3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410223 Commit-Ready: Matthew S Atwood &lt;matthew.s.atwood@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Waterlander &lt;patrick.waterlander@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mohammed Habibulla &lt;moch@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="410223" owner_email="matthew.s.atwood@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/23/410223/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifd5a86eeda5e7c5cef2e9c80df08bff3b7b40575" commit="479fef8763c748b27b16682c2fd5e0b712e7a0cb" commit_mes